0. Definitions

"Runtime Library" means the runtime of the programs made with LinBASIC Studio:
libvbrt, libvbforms and libvbdb, that is the files in the folder runtime/ of
LinBASIC Studio that bear this notice, with their header files (such as vbrt.h)
and the files made from them (generated .inc files, object files, static and
shared libraries: .a, .so, .dll, .def). Software of other authors that is in
that folder (SQLite, the Tiny C Compiler and its headers,
Qt) is not part of the Runtime Library and keeps its own license.

"Compiler Output" means the C source, object files and executables that the
LinBASIC Studio compiler (lbvc), or the IDE through it, produces from a
program's source, including the code that lbvc writes into that output.

"Program" means a work of a user (VB6-style projects, forms, modules, classes,
user controls, resources and any other code or data of the user) that is
compiled with LinBASIC Studio and combined with the Runtime Library, and
"Independent Modules" means the parts of a Program that are not derived from
the Runtime Library.


